        "original_id": "2ddf13d2-7694-5d00-a52f-de63eb7c2cea",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vincenzo Bellini, Mikhail Glinka\n- Roles: opera composer, composer\n- Places: Catania, Russia\n- Topics: Italian opera, Russian classical music\n\nFacts:\n- Vincenzo Bellini was born on 3 November 1801 and died on 23 September 1835.\n- Mikhail Glinka was born on 1 June 1804 (20 May O.S.) and died on 15 February 1857 (3 February O.S.).\n- Vincenzo Bellini was an Italian opera composer known for his long-flowing melodic lines.\n- Vincenzo Bellini was called \"the Swan of Catania.\"\n- Mikhail Glinka was the first Russian composer to gain wide recognition within Russia.\n- Mikhail Glinka is often regarded as the fountainhead of Russian classical music.",
